1
00:00:04,220 --> 00:00:06,380
It's my life. It's your life.

2
00:00:06,480 --> 00:00:07,697
Fighting for tomorrow.

3
00:00:07,780 --> 00:00:11,560
Go get what you really want.
I want more. Any one more.

4
00:00:11,720 --> 00:00:13,297
Come on, open up the door.

5
00:00:13,380 --> 00:00:15,540
It's my life. It's your life.

6
00:00:15,660 --> 00:00:17,060
Run like a winter fire.

7
00:00:17,520 --> 00:00:19,180
I know you're strong.

8
00:00:19,660 --> 00:00:21,700
Believe you can achieve your goal.

9
00:00:22,200 --> 00:00:23,376
Let's keep on going.

10
00:00:23,460 --> 00:00:24,400
I'll not stay.

11
00:00:44,460 --> 00:00:47,457
Let's do it again, you
know what I mean, baby.

12
00:00:47,540 --> 00:00:50,037
No one can make it my dream come true.

13
00:00:50,120 --> 00:00:52,717
Don't you feel it, I
really don't know what is.

14
00:00:52,800 --> 00:00:55,197
Something is testing me every day.

15
00:00:55,280 --> 00:00:56,557
Hey, let's go.

16
00:00:56,640 --> 00:00:57,477
Let's fly away.

17
00:00:57,560 --> 00:01:00,577
I know I never wanna come back here.

18
00:01:00,660 --> 00:01:01,797
Hey, let's go.

19
00:01:01,880 --> 00:01:02,717
Let's fly away.

20
00:01:02,800 --> 00:01:05,597
The great end of the unknown rules.

21
00:01:05,680 --> 00:01:07,437
Standing up, blowing up.

22
00:01:07,520 --> 00:01:09,657
My dream is getting wilder.

23
00:01:09,740 --> 00:01:12,617
I'm not afraid, beat me, hit me.

24
00:01:12,700 --> 00:01:15,137
I will never turn around.

25
00:01:15,220 --> 00:01:17,917
Another day, another chance.

26
00:01:18,000 --> 00:01:20,097
You know it's never too late.

27
00:01:20,180 --> 00:01:22,400
If I can do it, so can you.

28
00:01:26,040 --> 00:01:28,477
It's my life, it's your life.

29
00:01:28,560 --> 00:01:29,597
Fight if you can't

30
00:01:29,680 --> 00:01:30,510
achieve

31
00:01:30,593 --> 00:01:36,980
your

32
00:01:44,660 --> 00:01:45,490
goal.

33
00:01:45,573 --> 00:01:47,057
Let's keep on going, roaring.

34
00:01:47,140 --> 00:01:49,377
It's my life, it's your life.

35
00:01:49,460 --> 00:01:52,457
Fighting for your eyes that
I want, but you really want.

36
00:01:52,540 --> 00:01:57,337
I want more, anyone more,
come on, open up the gate.

37
00:01:57,420 --> 00:02:01,537
It's my life, it's your life,
shine like a star to be good.

38
00:02:01,620 --> 00:02:06,257
I know you're strong, just that
you can't achieve your best.

39
00:02:06,340 --> 00:02:08,540
Let's keep on going, I love this.

40
00:02:15,420 --> 00:02:19,020
You make my day every day.

41
00:02:49,640 --> 00:02:54,300
Now, little people, are
you guys ready to wreck?

42
00:02:57,600 --> 00:03:00,520
This factory made you
don't tell to suffer.

43
00:03:00,840 --> 00:03:03,380
It's time to collect your payback.

44
00:03:03,680 --> 00:03:04,617
Bust it.

45
00:03:04,700 --> 00:03:06,460
AHHHHH!

46
00:03:18,040 --> 00:03:20,440
Good luck, little bros.

47
00:03:24,780 --> 00:03:30,120
The rest of this is in your hands, Luffy.

48
00:03:45,320 --> 00:03:47,740
Send the rescue team over here!

49
00:03:47,920 --> 00:03:49,800
There's injured people! Sir!

50
00:03:57,720 --> 00:03:58,550
Showtime!

51
00:03:58,633 --> 00:03:59,463
Mwah!

52
00:04:02,840 --> 00:04:07,320
Half moon flavor!

53
00:04:13,040 --> 00:04:13,870
Kiddos!

54
00:04:14,080 --> 00:04:17,860
I thought you had it up
to here with me before.

55
00:04:18,260 --> 00:04:20,560
What happened to all the big talk, huh?

56
00:04:21,860 --> 00:04:25,397
Did you really think I
was just a gifted matador

57
00:04:25,480 --> 00:04:28,440
whose name sends ripples
through the stadium?

58
00:04:28,920 --> 00:04:32,220
You may have been the strongest
competitor at one point,

59
00:04:32,320 --> 00:04:34,555
but that wasn't meant to last forever.

60
00:04:34,700 --> 00:04:37,900
I astound all while
slaying the competition.

61
00:04:38,260 --> 00:04:40,780
The current hero of the Coliseum

62
00:04:41,680 --> 00:04:44,280
is the brilliant Diamante!

63
00:04:45,840 --> 00:04:49,440
Did you really think I
was just a gifted matador?

64
00:04:49,660 --> 00:04:51,700
The title means nothing to me!

65
00:04:52,220 --> 00:04:54,620
Fame can be evasive, I know!

66
00:05:04,960 --> 00:05:05,980
Be careful.

67
00:05:07,320 --> 00:05:08,960
A fine attempt.

68
00:05:09,200 --> 00:05:10,740
You almost had me.

69
00:05:15,120 --> 00:05:16,660
I can't blame you.

70
00:05:16,920 --> 00:05:19,802
You have been running
around the kingdom all day.

71
00:05:20,220 --> 00:05:23,357
Then you gotta protect your daughter
and the ground's all wobbly.

72
00:05:23,440 --> 00:05:24,540
Life's crazy.

73
00:05:26,220 --> 00:05:29,717
I'm afraid you're a day late
and a leg short, my man.

74
00:05:29,800 --> 00:05:31,940
Anyone would be at the limit by now.

75
00:05:32,240 --> 00:05:35,640
Only a fool would patronize me for my leg.

76
00:05:36,580 --> 00:05:37,410
Really?

77
00:05:39,260 --> 00:05:43,340
If I were to use that as an excuse,
I would then have come here.

78
00:05:43,560 --> 00:05:44,780
I take great pride.

79
00:05:45,240 --> 00:05:48,780
It was a small sacrifice
for the man who saved me.

80
00:05:49,020 --> 00:05:53,237
If you say so, I won't feel guilty
about attacking your weak spot.

81
00:05:53,320 --> 00:05:55,837
But it won't be any fun for me to utterly

82
00:05:55,920 --> 00:05:58,580
crush you while you
need your nappy whappy.

83
00:05:58,820 --> 00:05:59,938
So what do you say?

84
00:06:00,960 --> 00:06:03,760
How about we pass the
time with the game, huh?

85
00:06:08,160 --> 00:06:12,180
And now, the last showtime!

86
00:06:17,560 --> 00:06:18,720
It's confetti.

87
00:06:19,000 --> 00:06:19,980
It's just paper?

88
00:06:20,660 --> 00:06:21,877
Confetti? Yes!

89
00:06:21,960 --> 00:06:26,257
paper, no, I wonder what
the mystery item could be,

90
00:06:26,340 --> 00:06:32,980
and now for my next
trick, ripple, release.

91
00:06:35,600 --> 00:06:39,617
spiky metal balls—look at
the breathtaking sights!

92
00:06:39,700 --> 00:06:42,837
It's like falling stardust, Robin!

93
00:06:42,920 --> 00:06:47,197
We have no place to hide,
Robiland—protect Rebecca!

94
00:06:47,280 --> 00:06:50,157
You're in danger too, commander!

95
00:06:50,240 --> 00:06:52,897
Do not waste concern on me!

96
00:06:52,980 --> 00:06:56,897
What a great view the last one you'll see?

97
00:06:56,980 --> 00:07:01,917
I hate to boast, but my stardust
can wipe out an entire army,

98
00:07:02,000 --> 00:07:05,057
and it's nearly impossible to survive!

99
00:07:05,140 --> 00:07:09,040
to survive Luckily, we are in this field.

100
00:07:10,060 --> 00:07:11,080
Meal fluid!

101
00:07:14,360 --> 00:07:16,860
Forgive me, flowers.

102
00:07:20,980 --> 00:07:23,600
It's too bad you're not under here.

103
00:07:24,820 --> 00:07:26,260
Adios, pal!

104
00:07:26,820 --> 00:07:29,000
Death and hungry!

105
00:07:36,880 --> 00:07:38,300
Blower Umbrella!

106
00:07:39,960 --> 00:07:41,620
That was a close one.

107
00:07:42,100 --> 00:07:44,040
Oh, not too shabby.

108
00:07:44,760 --> 00:07:45,590
Pay attention.

109
00:07:50,180 --> 00:07:51,400
Kittles, wow!

110
00:07:51,780 --> 00:07:55,839
Any army that would fall through
this trickery surely lacks training.

111
00:07:56,320 --> 00:07:57,680
This is insanity!

112
00:07:58,380 --> 00:08:01,420
How are you smacking my
stardust away mid-air?

113
00:08:03,040 --> 00:08:06,360
Can you also walk through
rain without getting wet?

114
00:08:06,660 --> 00:08:07,580
Fine, then.

115
00:08:19,120 --> 00:08:20,460
Mother, no!

116
00:08:23,540 --> 00:08:26,040
The sky's falling, kiddos.

117
00:08:26,260 --> 00:08:30,857
I bet you wouldn't have stumbled if you
still had that extra leg right about now.

118
00:08:30,940 --> 00:08:33,740
You can't do this to him! Diamante!

119
00:08:33,840 --> 00:08:34,840
Stop it, Rebecca!

120
00:08:35,080 --> 00:08:36,786
Please stay under the canopy!

121
00:08:38,060 --> 00:08:39,200
Father, no!

122
00:08:40,040 --> 00:08:40,870
You bastard!

123
00:08:41,460 --> 00:08:44,100
I will never forgive
you for this, Diamante!

124
00:08:45,540 --> 00:08:47,420
Fine, then don't forgive me!

125
00:08:47,680 --> 00:08:48,920
Come make me pay!

126
00:08:49,440 --> 00:08:50,880
You want a piece?

127
00:08:51,040 --> 00:08:52,760
I got a bullet for you!

128
00:08:53,260 --> 00:08:55,000
Just like your mommy!

129
00:08:55,400 --> 00:08:56,777
Please unhand me, Robin!

130
00:08:56,860 --> 00:08:58,440
I have to kill this man!

131
00:09:05,100 --> 00:09:08,688
I'm not sure how much more the
Flower Umbrella can withstand.

132
00:09:11,760 --> 00:09:13,700
Damn you! No way!

133
00:09:28,420 --> 00:09:30,117
Lower your weapon right now!

134
00:09:30,200 --> 00:09:35,880
Now, Rebecca, this is my fight.

135
00:09:38,320 --> 00:09:43,540
Ten years, you have suffered
on your own. Come here.

136
00:09:43,740 --> 00:09:44,916
You need to recover.

137
00:09:45,120 --> 00:09:46,080
You'll die.

138
00:09:46,320 --> 00:09:50,520
For ten years, you've
upheld your mother's wish.

139
00:09:51,760 --> 00:09:55,217
My mother told me I should never
hurt others, no matter what.

140
00:09:55,300 --> 00:09:58,829
But you must protect yourself
from those who would hurt you.

141
00:09:59,580 --> 00:10:02,320
Rebecca has never once wounded anybody!

142
00:10:02,820 --> 00:10:07,140
So far, she's won every buck just by
letting her foes fall off the side!

143
00:10:08,260 --> 00:10:10,680
You only win by disqualification!

144
00:10:11,360 --> 00:10:13,320
Chance of blood, you weakling!

145
00:10:13,440 --> 00:10:15,320
You're a huge coward! Boo!

146
00:10:15,800 --> 00:10:18,035
You should be ashamed of your victory.

147
00:10:18,600 --> 00:10:21,500
There's no way a gladiator
should claim glory.

148
00:10:22,080 --> 00:10:24,660
I hope you get stabbed this time!

149
00:10:24,840 --> 00:10:25,977
You're a descendant of evil!

150
00:10:26,060 --> 00:10:27,680
You're nothing but garbage!

151
00:10:31,700 --> 00:10:36,780
though you fought in the coliseum
you still haven't harmed a soul

152
00:10:38,500 --> 00:10:43,980
your hands are still clean they're
untainted your mother's heart

153
00:10:46,380 --> 00:10:49,240
reside in those pristine hands

154
00:10:55,280 --> 00:10:56,110
mother

155
00:10:58,160 --> 00:11:04,120
so i will not allow for you to
stain them with this lousy's blood

156
00:11:10,680 --> 00:11:15,300
from now on you will
live your life peacefully

157
00:11:29,780 --> 00:11:31,280
What the hell?

158
00:11:32,160 --> 00:11:33,860
How are you standing?

159
00:11:34,260 --> 00:11:35,640
Are you solid steel?

160
00:11:40,240 --> 00:11:41,520
Come on.

161
00:11:41,740 --> 00:11:43,220
You're crazy.

162
00:11:43,740 --> 00:11:45,140
No, I take that back.

163
00:11:52,520 --> 00:11:53,600
This pain.

164
00:11:55,040 --> 00:11:57,620
Is proof that I am human.

165
00:11:58,160 --> 00:12:01,400
You wouldn't understand, you monster!

166
00:12:03,940 --> 00:12:08,560
This is nothing compared to
the grief of being forgotten.

167
00:12:11,240 --> 00:12:12,070
Skirtlet.

168
00:12:13,780 --> 00:12:16,000
Damn it, why did you wait for me?

169
00:12:16,340 --> 00:12:17,700
Why are you here?

170
00:12:19,640 --> 00:12:21,140
I see now.

171
00:12:22,200 --> 00:12:25,200
It seems I've been erased
from everyone's memories.

172
00:12:25,640 --> 00:12:27,120
Our promises.

173
00:12:28,320 --> 00:12:29,560
Our time together.

174
00:12:30,760 --> 00:12:31,590
Gone.

175
00:12:32,060 --> 00:12:33,760
My daughter is hungry.

176
00:12:34,080 --> 00:12:35,740
And she's waiting for me.

177
00:12:36,340 --> 00:12:37,620
I'm your husband.

178
00:12:38,100 --> 00:12:39,240
I beg you.

179
00:12:44,320 --> 00:12:46,737
These useless tin arms of mine.

180
00:12:46,820 --> 00:12:50,860
I can't even feel your
warmth one last time!

181
00:13:01,740 --> 00:13:05,297
You'll never be able
to grasp the unbearable

182
00:13:05,380 --> 00:13:08,660
ache of being unable to
feel anything you touch!

183
00:13:09,200 --> 00:13:13,917
Compared to all the despicable acts you
committed against the people of Dressrosa,

184
00:13:14,000 --> 00:13:17,857
what I suffer now is scarcely pain at all

185
00:13:17,940 --> 00:13:22,777
if I'm sure that

186
00:13:22,860 --> 00:13:27,317
anything and I am this

187
00:13:27,400 --> 00:13:34,017
kingdom solid rage
manifested here to collect

188
00:13:34,100 --> 00:13:34,957
pay back

189
00:13:35,040 --> 00:13:39,317
you

190
00:13:39,400 --> 00:13:43,337
were in

191
00:13:43,420 --> 00:13:44,577
your prime two decades?

192
00:13:44,660 --> 00:13:47,340
You should have peaked by now!

193
00:13:50,780 --> 00:13:53,180
Don't overlook my sword skills!

194
00:13:53,640 --> 00:13:54,680
You fool!

195
00:13:58,680 --> 00:14:01,080
You ready to call the curtains yet?

196
00:14:01,300 --> 00:14:03,117
I'll show you to your grave!

197
00:14:03,200 --> 00:14:04,320
Whoa!

198
00:14:13,200 --> 00:14:15,920
Looks like my metal rain cleared up.

199
00:14:18,320 --> 00:14:22,100
I suppose it's more fitting
if I finish you off myself.

200
00:14:23,180 --> 00:14:27,700
Just like I did with Scarlet, and
I bet you miss her, don't you?

201
00:14:39,040 --> 00:14:41,817
So cruel he keeps taunting them,

202
00:14:41,900 --> 00:14:47,520
laughing about scarlet's death,
like rubbing salt in a wound.

203
00:14:50,080 --> 00:14:52,297
I'm sorry, king Rick;

204
00:14:52,380 --> 00:14:57,317
our searches ended in vain—a man
named diamante got ahead of our party.

205
00:14:57,400 --> 00:14:58,230
party

206
00:14:58,620 --> 00:15:03,300
Scarlet was found in the town,
but she was killed by gunshot.

207
00:15:07,780 --> 00:15:09,360
You killed Scarlet?

208
00:15:09,560 --> 00:15:10,420
Oh, yeah?

209
00:15:10,760 --> 00:15:12,740
That was your older sister, huh?

210
00:15:13,200 --> 00:15:17,140
It's such a shame she had to go
and buy food at the market today.

211
00:15:17,460 --> 00:15:21,337
If she could have controlled her
hunger, she wouldn't have been killed.

212
00:15:21,420 --> 00:15:22,880
What a greedy sow.

213
00:15:23,860 --> 00:15:25,420
Jake, let go of me!

214
00:15:25,700 --> 00:15:27,317
Please don't act in haste.

215
00:15:27,400 --> 00:15:29,137
You must think rationally!

216
00:15:29,220 --> 00:15:30,400
Just let me go!

217
00:15:31,260 --> 00:15:32,280
Help me out!

218
00:15:32,480 --> 00:15:34,068
We must stay in the palace!

219
00:15:35,240 --> 00:15:36,946
It's for your own protection!

220
00:15:53,840 --> 00:15:55,657
You don't know how this ends!

221
00:15:55,740 --> 00:15:59,680
My next strike is strong
enough to shatter the earth!

222
00:16:03,800 --> 00:16:05,080
Take this!

223
00:16:05,980 --> 00:16:06,810
This!

224
00:16:08,900 --> 00:16:13,560
Think that wounded leg can dodge
what I am about to throw at you?

225
00:16:15,040 --> 00:16:16,600
I will not dodge.

226
00:16:16,820 --> 00:16:17,660
A thing!

227
00:16:18,020 --> 00:16:21,920
If you're not gonna avoid my attack,
then you're just a damn fool!

228
00:16:22,480 --> 00:16:24,237
Now I'm taking our peace back!

229
00:16:24,320 --> 00:16:25,720
Half moon.

230
00:16:31,600 --> 00:16:32,440
Treno.

231
00:16:59,400 --> 00:17:00,800
Shit.

232
00:17:27,400 --> 00:17:30,280
You have my gratitude, Robiland.

233
00:17:58,280 --> 00:17:59,110
Father!

234
00:18:02,700 --> 00:18:03,530
Father!

235
00:18:03,613 --> 00:18:05,459
Father, you need to get patched up.

236
00:18:12,460 --> 00:18:14,820
I could not save your mother's life,

237
00:18:15,120 --> 00:18:18,580
but I'll devote mine to protect
yours, whatever the cost.

238
00:18:20,620 --> 00:18:25,940
Someday, happiness will return to
you, Until then, I'll stay right here.

239
00:18:47,080 --> 00:18:49,320
He defeated Diamante!

240
00:18:53,820 --> 00:18:54,650
Crazy.

241
00:18:54,980 --> 00:18:56,215
He took down someone.

242
00:18:56,300 --> 00:18:57,160
So strong.

243
00:19:06,620 --> 00:19:08,320
But how is Kiros, though?

244
00:19:08,700 --> 00:19:09,818
Does he still live?

245
00:19:10,500 --> 00:19:11,330
He lives.

246
00:19:11,413 --> 00:19:13,360
Kiros is injured, but safe.

247
00:19:14,180 --> 00:19:15,377
And Rebecca, too.

248
00:19:15,460 --> 00:19:18,560
It's thanks to Nico
Robin that she survived.

249
00:19:20,520 --> 00:19:24,402
It's unbelievable that he took out
the top Don Quixote executives!

250
00:19:24,840 --> 00:19:27,480
And the Coliseum Hero at that!

251
00:19:28,160 --> 00:19:29,100
Is that a joke?

252
00:19:29,380 --> 00:19:33,615
You must have forgotten that Kiros
was the original undefeated champion!

253
00:19:36,440 --> 00:19:39,597
We truly thought the Don
Quixote family was invincible,

254
00:19:39,680 --> 00:19:42,327
but here they are dropping
one after another!

255
00:19:48,560 --> 00:19:53,060
He did well that's our commander

256
00:20:01,940 --> 00:20:05,240
Now the tables are turning
in our favor at last

257
00:20:06,020 --> 00:20:08,977
The warriors recruited by
this Straw Hat pirates have

258
00:20:09,060 --> 00:20:12,413
taken down the lower-ranking
executives one after another

259
00:20:13,900 --> 00:20:17,547
There's only four major players
of the Don Quixote family left

260
00:20:20,060 --> 00:20:25,020
Bellamy the hyena, then two high-ranking
executives, Pika, and Treble.

261
00:20:25,700 --> 00:20:31,440
After that, only the current king and
warlord of the sea, Doflamingo, remains.

262
00:20:33,080 --> 00:20:33,910
That's it.

263
00:20:33,993 --> 00:20:35,360
Our final hurdle!

264
00:20:39,880 --> 00:20:42,000
I never thought they'd get this far.

265
00:20:42,440 --> 00:20:44,499
These Straw Hat people are amazing!

266
00:20:44,840 --> 00:20:47,297
I can't believe we tried
to kill these magnificent

267
00:20:47,380 --> 00:20:49,792
bastards in an attempt to save ourselves!

268
00:20:50,180 --> 00:20:52,997
Well, there's no use crying
over spilt milk, right?

269
00:20:53,080 --> 00:20:55,637
Plus, you guys are saying
such nice stuff about us now.

270
00:20:55,720 --> 00:20:57,320
I can't stay mad at you.

271
00:20:59,760 --> 00:21:02,701
Old King Rick, where are
you going, Your Highness?

272
00:21:03,340 --> 00:21:06,281
I do not believe my life
is threatened any longer.

273
00:21:06,580 --> 00:21:07,860
I'm going to town.

274
00:21:08,180 --> 00:21:10,440
There is still much left to be done.

275
00:21:11,840 --> 00:21:13,620
Allow me to escort you, sir.

276
00:21:14,280 --> 00:21:17,515
I have very little faith in
the government or the Navy.

277
00:21:18,860 --> 00:21:20,617
Everyone's feeling helpless right now.

278
00:21:20,700 --> 00:21:24,440
They think there's no escaping
the sick game or the birdcage.

279
00:21:25,320 --> 00:21:26,920
I say we all go.

280
00:21:28,700 --> 00:21:31,876
Let's spread a message of
hope throughout the kingdom.

281
00:21:36,780 --> 00:21:40,604
It seems we have finally captured
what one would call a breather.

282
00:21:43,480 --> 00:21:47,240
Hey, where did that one
Navy admiral guy go anyway?

283
00:21:47,660 --> 00:21:49,601
Did you not take note, Sir Usopp?

284
00:21:49,700 --> 00:21:52,818
That decorated fellow traveled
into town a while ago.

285
00:21:53,180 --> 00:21:57,000
In that case, gather up all the
civilians you can to one place.

286
00:21:58,740 --> 00:22:00,377
Make certain it's secure.

287
00:22:00,460 --> 00:22:03,160
We will keep them all safe. Sir!

288
00:22:07,440 --> 00:22:08,400
The hell?

289
00:22:11,360 --> 00:22:13,180
That bastard.

290
00:22:16,680 --> 00:22:18,000
Hey, father.

291
00:22:18,360 --> 00:22:19,536
What's that shaking?

292
00:22:24,920 --> 00:22:25,960
Rebecca!

293
00:22:27,860 --> 00:22:28,900
No!

294
00:22:29,420 --> 00:22:30,920
I thought Zoro had him.

295
00:22:31,460 --> 00:22:32,360
That's Pika.

296
00:22:38,020 --> 00:22:39,060
Killer?

297
00:22:42,640 --> 00:22:43,840
Oh, Diamante!

298
00:22:44,720 --> 00:22:48,700
That's a real bad look for a
top executive in our family!

299
00:23:00,460 --> 00:23:01,290
Father!

300
00:23:03,320 --> 00:23:08,940
As foreseen, I did not come here
for a mere one-on-one skirmish.

301
00:23:10,240 --> 00:23:13,040
As long as an enemy
stands, the fight persists.

302
00:23:14,760 --> 00:23:16,200
You can barely move.

303
00:23:16,520 --> 00:23:17,755
Please don't do this.

304
00:23:17,880 --> 00:23:18,998
Fall back, Rebecca.

305
00:23:19,320 --> 00:23:20,420
Quick question.

306
00:23:21,020 --> 00:23:24,240
Why is old King Rick worth
a squat to you people?

307
00:23:25,480 --> 00:23:29,540
Rebecca, isn't he the reason
why everybody hates you so much?

308
00:23:32,180 --> 00:23:34,137
Why do you respect that puke?

309
00:23:34,220 --> 00:23:35,161
That's nonsense.

310
00:23:35,260 --> 00:23:37,177
You despicable people framed him.

311
00:23:37,260 --> 00:23:41,120
My father-in-law is my personal savior.

312
00:23:41,560 --> 00:23:44,240
He showed benevolence
to this young ruffian.

313
00:23:45,200 --> 00:23:49,357
The Rick bloodline upheld
a reputation for being

314
00:23:49,440 --> 00:23:52,028
a family that understood
the value of peace.

315
00:23:55,020 --> 00:23:59,140
Our richness came from
routine joys, clear skies,

316
00:23:59,560 --> 00:24:02,880
thriving blossoms, a
kingdom of gentle hearts.

317
00:24:03,160 --> 00:24:05,689
That's the backbone on
which we flourished.

318
00:24:08,600 --> 00:24:11,437
Our entire nation wishes for your wicked

319
00:24:11,520 --> 00:24:14,820
family's swift removal
so he may reign again.

320
00:24:17,140 --> 00:24:18,240
I see!

321
00:24:21,840 --> 00:24:22,670
Huh?

322
00:24:22,753 --> 00:24:23,583
He left.

323
00:24:31,260 --> 00:24:32,090
The hell?

324
00:24:32,173 --> 00:24:33,864
That scared the crap out of me!

325
00:24:34,180 --> 00:24:36,062
Pika escaped to the third level.

326
00:24:37,940 --> 00:24:39,560
What a pain in the ass.

327
00:24:39,700 --> 00:24:41,229
He's supposed to fight me.

328
00:24:41,600 --> 00:24:43,129
Why is he in such a hurry?

329
00:24:49,640 --> 00:24:51,897
How am I supposed to
knock the snot out of him

330
00:24:51,980 --> 00:24:54,568
when he's scurrying
around like a damn mole?

331
00:24:55,080 --> 00:24:57,540
As soon as I close in on him, he's done.

332
00:24:57,740 --> 00:24:58,620
Just go!

333
00:25:00,080 --> 00:25:02,320
Lord Pika, please have mercy on us!

334
00:25:02,800 --> 00:25:04,600
You forget we're on your team!

335
00:25:11,840 --> 00:25:14,400
Hunting the injured, spineless prick!

336
00:25:14,820 --> 00:25:17,620
You've betrayed the family, BB-5!

337
00:25:18,020 --> 00:25:18,917
Steal me!

338
00:25:19,000 --> 00:25:19,860
Watch out!

339
00:25:25,080 --> 00:25:25,910
Trilestone!

340
00:25:34,680 --> 00:25:36,920
That big, shrill bastard!

341
00:25:38,320 --> 00:25:40,120
You're pissing me off!

342
00:25:40,280 --> 00:25:41,620
Cut the crap already!

343
00:25:42,020 --> 00:25:44,217
Stop going after all the wounded people!

344
00:25:44,300 --> 00:25:45,440
I'm over here!

345
00:25:46,180 --> 00:25:47,010
Light stone!

346
00:25:47,280 --> 00:25:48,520
One sword style.

347
00:25:48,780 --> 00:25:49,660
Demon horse!

348
00:25:50,560 --> 00:25:52,800
You know, Roranora Zoro,

349
00:25:53,140 --> 00:25:56,728
there's a very important someone
up on the King's Black Zone!

350
00:25:57,300 --> 00:25:59,760
The King of Dressrosa? Thorma!

351
00:26:00,500 --> 00:26:02,680
Get to the point, soprano man!

352
00:26:05,020 --> 00:26:08,255
Aside from the has-been king
and some of his followers,

353
00:26:08,520 --> 00:26:12,873
I heard the samurai and god Usuf are
on the king's plateau right now, too.

354
00:26:13,960 --> 00:26:16,020
So, if I understand correctly,

355
00:26:16,280 --> 00:26:19,857
suddenly the whole kingdom wants to
put King Rick back on the throne.

356
00:26:19,940 --> 00:26:21,300
Yeah, what's it to you?

357
00:26:21,560 --> 00:26:23,089
It pisses me off his what?

358
00:26:23,380 --> 00:26:25,380
Dolphy's the only one worthy here.

359
00:26:37,880 --> 00:26:39,280
What the hell?

360
00:26:50,840 --> 00:26:52,260
Son of a...

361
00:27:07,840 --> 00:27:10,200
Where's that big behemoth headed now?

362
00:27:10,520 --> 00:27:12,040
What is he gonna do?

363
00:27:19,620 --> 00:27:22,500
Dressrosa belongs to
the Don Quixote family!

364
00:27:27,240 --> 00:27:29,520
He's gonna walk! Let's go!

365
00:27:31,020 --> 00:27:33,960
The statue is moving! Run!

366
00:27:47,340 --> 00:27:49,240
Oh, jeez. Are you kidding me?

367
00:27:54,440 --> 00:27:55,640
Godless bastard!

368
00:27:56,160 --> 00:27:57,940
He's trying to kill the king.

369
00:28:02,420 --> 00:28:03,250
Damn it.

370
00:28:04,100 --> 00:28:06,865
That's why he ditched me
all the way back here.

371
00:28:08,400 --> 00:28:09,800
I can't catch up.

372
00:28:13,600 --> 00:28:15,520
I played right into his hands.

373
00:28:15,740 --> 00:28:17,622
Got to think fast of what to do.

374
00:28:19,240 --> 00:28:23,122
One quick punch from him and it
could take out the entire plateau.

375
00:28:23,680 --> 00:28:25,877
If I don't think of some
way to shut him down,

376
00:28:25,960 --> 00:28:28,237
Usopp and that king guy will
be crushed in an instant.

377
00:28:28,320 --> 00:28:32,220
Pirate Hunter, we won't let you
get any closer to Lord Pika.

378
00:28:36,380 --> 00:28:38,540
I don't have time for that crap.

379
00:28:40,740 --> 00:28:41,570
Zoro!

380
00:28:41,740 --> 00:28:43,387
He's controlling the statue.

381
00:28:43,840 --> 00:28:46,040
And headed for the King's Plateau.

382
00:28:51,060 --> 00:28:52,680
Grandfather. Who's up?

383
00:28:55,280 --> 00:28:56,110
Whoa!

384
00:28:56,193 --> 00:28:58,100
Hey, man, screw you!

385
00:29:03,440 --> 00:29:04,620
Plan one.

386
00:29:05,820 --> 00:29:07,460
Long distance slash.

387
00:29:15,560 --> 00:29:18,854
Now I'd have to travel too
far and it'd barely nick him.

388
00:29:20,980 --> 00:29:22,140
Plan two.

389
00:29:22,720 --> 00:29:24,480
Jump up and get on top.

390
00:29:28,960 --> 00:29:29,790
Impossible.

391
00:29:35,260 --> 00:29:36,480
Plan three.

392
00:29:37,060 --> 00:29:39,540
Shout out warning Usopp and the others.

393
00:29:43,120 --> 00:29:43,950
Usopp!

394
00:29:52,560 --> 00:29:54,157
No chance in hell.

395
00:29:54,240 --> 00:29:55,980
Not with all the noise.

396
00:30:00,060 --> 00:30:01,140
Plan four.

397
00:30:01,800 --> 00:30:05,329
Call him by transponder snail
and tell him hurry up and run.

398
00:30:15,240 --> 00:30:16,820
Oh, must have dropped it.

399
00:30:19,760 --> 00:30:21,480
Don't come any closer!

400
00:30:24,500 --> 00:30:26,757
Even if I do manage to
get the message out,

401
00:30:26,840 --> 00:30:29,252
there's not enough time for him to react.

402
00:30:38,480 --> 00:30:39,660
Smash it for good!

403
00:30:40,100 --> 00:30:41,140
Give him hell!

404
00:30:43,360 --> 00:30:45,320
He has his sights on King Rick.

405
00:30:47,440 --> 00:30:50,780
It's not our fight, but this
isn't sitting well with me.

406
00:30:50,920 --> 00:30:51,920
Stop right there!

407
00:30:52,240 --> 00:30:53,769
Don't do it, Snow Monster!

408
00:30:54,240 --> 00:30:57,097
The legendary sniper king
is on that very plateau.

409
00:30:57,180 --> 00:30:59,997
You, rock boy, you want to fight?

410
00:31:00,080 --> 00:31:02,197
Then I volunteer my. I

411
00:31:02,280 --> 00:31:09,280
see

412
00:31:19,600 --> 00:31:20,997
now the pirate hunter

413
00:31:21,080 --> 00:31:22,437
was a few steps ahead of us?

414
00:31:22,520 --> 00:31:24,932
Glad I saved my King Punch as he advised.

415
00:31:31,720 --> 00:31:34,140
I've got your back, Rick, my friend.

416
00:31:34,440 --> 00:31:35,640
Hey, King Punch guy!

417
00:31:36,980 --> 00:31:37,840
Excuse me?

418
00:31:38,000 --> 00:31:40,117
I'm Elisabello, the King of Prodents.

419
00:31:40,200 --> 00:31:42,318
I'd watch your tongue if I were you.

420
00:31:42,940 --> 00:31:45,587
I told you, trying to
shatter him won't work.

421
00:31:45,920 --> 00:31:48,997
You gotta hit his flesh and blood
or else he'll keep coming back.

422
00:31:49,080 --> 00:31:50,786
What are you suggesting then?

423
00:31:57,180 --> 00:32:00,140
I'll do anything, just save me!

424
00:32:02,820 --> 00:32:04,060
Pirate hunter?

425
00:32:30,920 --> 00:32:33,540
Well, give me two minutes.

426
00:32:35,240 --> 00:32:37,620
King Rick, you there?

427
00:32:43,420 --> 00:32:44,940
Plan five.

428
00:32:45,400 --> 00:32:47,740
Fly him to the sky and chop him up.

429
00:32:53,520 --> 00:32:55,480
Yep, that's the one.

430
00:33:12,380 --> 00:33:13,840
This looks dire.

431
00:33:14,180 --> 00:33:16,020
Grandfather's up there. Mr.

432
00:33:16,240 --> 00:33:17,140
Sniper King!

433
00:33:17,680 --> 00:33:19,180
Just run away!

434
00:33:29,360 --> 00:33:34,857
Hey pirate hunter, don't
make me wait too long, yo!

435
00:33:34,940 --> 00:33:38,157
Two by four, if you mean
Commodore—that's me!

436
00:33:38,240 --> 00:33:41,577
Yeah, whatever you're the guy
that threw that other guy?

437
00:33:41,660 --> 00:33:43,366
guy like a cannonball, right?

438
00:33:46,180 --> 00:33:49,060
Get smashed like a bug, Rick!

439
00:33:51,460 --> 00:33:52,780
Open fire!

440
00:34:06,120 --> 00:34:08,640
It is I you want. Face me.

441
00:34:09,360 --> 00:34:12,478
Do not put my people through
any more needless havoc.

442
00:34:16,020 --> 00:34:18,280
Everybody, it's time to flee!

443
00:34:18,740 --> 00:34:20,446
You must get off the plateau!

444
00:34:28,980 --> 00:34:30,500
Everyone has exited.

445
00:34:30,880 --> 00:34:32,040
It's your turn now.

446
00:34:33,020 --> 00:34:34,800
Father, hurry up!

447
00:34:35,060 --> 00:34:38,460
Viola and Tank, lead everyone to safety.

448
00:34:38,640 --> 00:34:41,680
He's only after me. Just go.

449
00:34:42,100 --> 00:34:43,629
You don't have to do this.

450
00:34:43,860 --> 00:34:45,880
King Rick, come with us.

451
00:34:46,300 --> 00:34:47,320
I can't.

452
00:34:47,500 --> 00:34:49,441
This may be the only opportunity.

453
00:34:50,260 --> 00:34:52,257
I am at peace with my choice.

454
00:34:52,340 --> 00:34:53,380
Now go, Tank.

455
00:34:55,320 --> 00:34:56,580
How sweet!

456
00:34:57,000 --> 00:35:00,460
Well, if that's what you
really want, I won't complain!

457
00:35:10,180 --> 00:35:11,440
What the hell?

458
00:35:11,960 --> 00:35:13,800
Pirate Hunter or Lumbus?

459
00:35:14,000 --> 00:35:15,437
What are you two plotting?

460
00:35:15,520 --> 00:35:17,477
You're certain you wish to do this?

461
00:35:17,560 --> 00:35:20,854
This technique is not meant
for throwing someone safely.

462
00:35:21,380 --> 00:35:22,397
Come on, carnivore.

463
00:35:22,480 --> 00:35:23,380
Just throw me.

464
00:35:23,700 --> 00:35:29,600
That bastard is only going after those
who won't fight back. You ready? Yeah.

465
00:35:33,360 --> 00:35:35,617
Rick, you're no king.

466
00:35:35,700 --> 00:35:38,640
You're not gonna have to lead anyone!

467
00:35:42,540 --> 00:35:43,370
Kumadori!

468
00:35:56,720 --> 00:35:58,860
If you won't run, neither will we.

469
00:35:59,240 --> 00:36:00,700
We stand with King Rick!

470
00:36:01,480 --> 00:36:02,477
Aw, Rick!

471
00:36:02,560 --> 00:36:06,480
Did your sheep forgive you for
that decade-long misunderstanding?

472
00:36:08,540 --> 00:36:11,920
How's a pacifist like you
gonna protect your kingdom?

473
00:36:12,460 --> 00:36:16,480
You couldn't even save
your own reputation, Rick.

474
00:36:18,060 --> 00:36:21,820
A kingdom's strength lies
in its military might.

475
00:36:22,160 --> 00:36:25,160
You know nothing about true authority.

476
00:36:26,360 --> 00:36:28,080
I'll crush you.

477
00:36:28,360 --> 00:36:29,960
I'll crush it all.

478
00:36:30,480 --> 00:36:31,677
ZEI!

479
00:36:31,760 --> 00:36:33,000
KING Rick!

480
00:36:36,840 --> 00:36:40,520
The town is going to pulverize me!

481
00:36:47,080 --> 00:36:48,440
KILLER!

482
00:36:49,180 --> 00:36:50,020
BOLING!

483
00:37:11,320 --> 00:37:12,837
What you say is true.

484
00:37:12,920 --> 00:37:14,857
I fail to protect my kingdom.

485
00:37:14,940 --> 00:37:17,580
I will never sit upon that throne again.

486
00:37:18,720 --> 00:37:19,550
However.

487
00:37:20,040 --> 00:37:21,477
To the bitter end.

488
00:37:21,560 --> 00:37:22,980
I will remain true.

489
00:37:28,980 --> 00:37:32,080
Nine mountains and eight
seas make one world.

490
00:37:33,980 --> 00:37:36,580
One thousand worlds make one Chilliocosm.

491
00:37:36,820 --> 00:37:39,460
One Chilliocosm to the power of three.

492
00:37:39,780 --> 00:37:41,860
And there's nothing I can't cut.

493
00:37:45,540 --> 00:37:47,599
Three-sword style secret technique.

494
00:37:48,340 --> 00:37:50,637
Are you naive or what?

495
00:37:50,720 --> 00:37:55,080
If the only means for me to survive
is becoming a cold-blooded killer,

496
00:37:55,360 --> 00:37:58,420
then I fearlessly choose death.

497
00:37:59,100 --> 00:38:01,747
There is no future for
a nation of slaughter.

498
00:38:02,320 --> 00:38:06,080
King Rick, we all
proudly stand behind you!

499
00:38:08,920 --> 00:38:12,980
Why do you think so many
do-gooders are lost to history?

500
00:38:13,660 --> 00:38:17,600
They always die off for
leaving a mark on the world!

501
00:38:21,780 --> 00:38:27,220
The billion-fold world
to kill your cousin!

502
00:39:09,160 --> 00:39:11,000
Good, he's in the top half.

503
00:39:11,540 --> 00:39:12,380
Rory Noah!

504
00:39:36,240 --> 00:39:38,020
Go, Zoro!

505
00:39:46,640 --> 00:39:48,560
Dead stones.

506
00:39:49,540 --> 00:39:50,657
Moving stones,

507
00:39:50,740 --> 00:39:55,517
it seems like his real body is shifting
to one of the newly sliced pieces.

508
00:39:55,600 --> 00:40:01,340
And every time I split him,
the other side dies off.

509
00:40:37,060 --> 00:40:40,295
As long as he's up here, he
can't burrow in the ground.

510
00:40:42,380 --> 00:40:44,280
Come on out! Peek up!

511
00:40:56,220 --> 00:40:58,926
How long are you going
to keep hiding from me?

512
00:41:00,120 --> 00:41:01,800
Soap by cornering me.

513
00:41:02,800 --> 00:41:04,560
You must think you've won.

514
00:41:11,480 --> 00:41:13,320
You've got it all figured out.

515
00:41:13,660 --> 00:41:16,317
Just cut some stones
and you can defeat me.

516
00:41:16,400 --> 00:41:20,840
Well, good luck cutting
through my Haki, you moron!

517
00:41:25,340 --> 00:41:27,060
A Haki user?

518
00:41:27,180 --> 00:41:30,700
Once I pound you into the
ground, it's all over for you!

519
00:41:35,080 --> 00:41:39,280
I don't have any more time to
waste on a pebble like you!

520
00:41:39,620 --> 00:41:40,540
Take that back!

521
00:41:44,060 --> 00:41:46,380
Nine mountains and eight seas.

522
00:41:46,760 --> 00:41:48,580
There's nothing I can't cut.

523
00:41:48,740 --> 00:41:49,920
Right in hell!

524
00:41:50,720 --> 00:41:51,880
Uranoa, Zoro!

525
00:41:52,800 --> 00:41:54,760
Three thousand worlds!

526
00:41:59,160 --> 00:42:02,000
Now quit picking on the innocent, will ya?

527
00:42:03,180 --> 00:42:05,340
What an upstanding guy!

528
00:42:06,500 --> 00:42:07,330
Zoro!

529
00:42:11,980 --> 00:42:15,480
He really did it, it's over!

530
00:42:15,880 --> 00:42:17,660
He saved my friend, Rick!

531
00:42:24,540 --> 00:42:25,370
Oh crap!

532
